{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass when Rachel had borne Joseph.</b> That is, when the days of his servitude were completed, for all the tribes were born during the last seven years, and Rachel gave birth last, as it is written, ״ורחל עקרה״ (and Rachel was barren). And when Joseph was born, the fourteen years of his servitude were completed; therefore <b>and he said: send me away and I will go</b>, etc. Another interpretation: <b>and he said: send me away</b> — but before Joseph was born Jacob did not ask permission, for perhaps he would not grant permission and would not let them go with him, because he feared to say: he may hate her and divorce her, since she was barren. We learned there in Seder Olam: eleven tribes and Dinah — all were born during seven years, each one at seven months. The explanation: for each one, six months of pregnancy and a week of impurity. And thus it is established: one who gives birth at seven months gives birth at incomplete months."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:46.439456058Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}